/target
Cargo.lock
# Generated from Cargo.toml.example by the module's build step. It is NOT committed
# on purpose: a file named `Cargo.toml` anywhere in the bohay repo makes
# `cargo install --git <bohay>` see two binary packages (bohay + bohay-buzz) and
# refuse to pick one. Shipping the manifest as `.example` and generating this at
# build time keeps the top-level install unambiguous.
/Cargo.toml
